invariant: INV-26
file: gcm.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: an AES=runtime QUIC object runs GHASH on the carry-less multiply
  for a schedule the table runs, so a session whose caller's probe found
  no AES instructions executes PMULL or PCLMULQDQ on every Initial packet.
  Both GHASH bodies compute the same bytes, so no vector notices.
  bin/aes_runtime_test counts the calls into ghash_hw.c under the absent
  answer and requires none.

--- old
    return k->instructions == CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_PRESENT;
--- new
    return k->instructions != 0;
